<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5. </span>Error Analysis and Stability Controls</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error propagation analysis.</span>
To understand how prediction errors affect the output, we analyze how errors propagate through the denoising trajectory. When SCOPE uses <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Predict</span> mode, the predicted velocity <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from the true velocity <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and this error compounds over multiple steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{v}=\lVert\hat{v}_{k}-v_{k}\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{v}=\lVert\hat{v}_{k}-v_{k}\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the prediction error on velocity and let <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{x}=\lVert\hat{x}_{k}-x_{k}\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{x}=\lVert\hat{x}_{k}-x_{k}\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the latent-state error before step <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. From the Euler update in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1. Preliminaries ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Not All Frames Deserve Full Computation: Accelerating Autoregressive Video Generation via Selective Computation and Predictive Extrapolation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the one-step latent drift satisfies:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k-1}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+|\Delta\sigma_{k}|e_{k}^{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k-1}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+|\Delta\sigma_{k}|e_{k}^{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This shows that each prediction error <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes to the latent error proportionally to the step size <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\sigma_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\sigma_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>. After <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive predicted steps, the cumulative error becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k-h}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}|\Delta\sigma_{k-i}|e_{k-i}^{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k-h}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}|\Delta\sigma_{k-i}|e_{k-i}^{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If the local first-order predictor obeys a Taylor remainder bound <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}^{v}\leq\frac{L_{2}}{2}|\Delta\sigma_{k}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}^{v}\leq\frac{L_{2}}{2}|\Delta\sigma_{k}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k-h}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+\frac{L_{2}}{2}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}|\Delta\sigma_{k-i}|^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k-h}^{x}\leq e_{k}^{x}+\frac{L_{2}}{2}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}|\Delta\sigma_{k-i}|^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This bound reveals that the error grows cubically with step size, motivating three complementary stability controls.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability controls.</span>
First, after each <span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Predict</span> step the discrepancy score is damped by a decay factor <math id="S3.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}=\lambda r_{k}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}=\lambda r_{k}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, steering the system toward a <span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Recompute</span> step before drift becomes excessive. Second, the maximum number of consecutive non-<span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Recompute</span> steps is capped at <math id="S3.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, guaranteeing periodic updates regardless of the current discrepancy score. Third, every <span id="S3.SS5.p7.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Recompute</span> step resets the discrepancy score to <math id="S3.SS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and refreshes the velocity cache, preventing error propagation across recompute boundaries. The full derivation is deferred to the supplementary material.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02979v1/x1.png" id="S3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197" alt="Representative qualitative comparison across all methods on the two target models, with each row annotated by its speedup on SkyReels-V2 and MAGI-1.">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative comparison of all methods on representative prompts from the two models. The left two groups show results on SkyReels-V2, while the right group shows results on MAGI-1. Each method row is annotated with its end-to-end speedup on SkyReels-V2 and MAGI-1, respectively. Compared with other accelerated baselines, SCOPE preserves object structure and visual fidelity more consistently while maintaining the strongest overall acceleration-quality tradeoff.</span><span id="acmlabel5" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Representative qualitative comparison across all methods on the two target models, with each row annotated by its speedup on SkyReels-V2 and MAGI-1.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2604.02979v1/fig_exp5_blueviolet_BP5_20260320_134714.svg" id="S3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197" aria-label="Decision timeline visualization showing cache, predict, and recompute mode distributions across denoising iterations for both MAGI-1 and SkyReels-V2."><p>Decision timeline visualization showing cache, predict, and recompute mode distributions across denoising iterations for both MAGI-1 and SkyReels-V2.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="S3.F6.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Tri-modal decision timeline comparison between SkyReels-V2 (top) and MAGI-1 (bottom). Each row shows the <span id="S3.F6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Cache</span>, <span id="S3.F6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Predict</span>, and <span id="S3.F6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Recompute</span> decisions across denoising iterations.</span><span id="acmlabel6" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Decision timeline visualization showing cache, predict, and recompute mode distributions across denoising iterations for both MAGI-1 and SkyReels-V2.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section evaluates SCOPE on two representative AR diffusion models. We organize the experiments around the speed-quality tradeoff and the model-specific contribution of each technical line, reporting both quantitative comparisons and qualitative results.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Models, Dataset, and Metrics</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate SCOPE on two autoregressive video diffusion models. <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SkyReels-V2 DF-1.3B</span>: we use the 540P diffusion-forcing model with the aligned benchmark configuration that generates 257-frame videos with a base window of 97 frames, 50 denoising steps, and overlap history 17. <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MAGI-1 4.5B-distill</span>: we use the aligned distill runtime configuration with 240 frames at 480<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>480 resolution and 64 denoising steps. KV offload remains disabled so that the Original and accelerated runs share the same basic generation setup.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The prompts are drawn from the VBench gallery <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, spanning 16 evaluation dimensions. All accelerated methods match the Original pipeline exactly in frame count, resolution, denoising steps, seeds, and AR settings. A run is valid only after checking for failure modes such as black screens, frozen output, or severe artifacts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span>Sensitivity analysis across threshold settings on both models. Each configuration is denoted as <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{c},\tau_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{c},\tau_{p})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cache threshold and <math id="S4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is the prediction threshold.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.8" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.8.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.8.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Config <math id="S4.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{c},\tau_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{c},\tau_{p})</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="S4.T2.8.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Efficiency</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.8.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quality</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.8.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.8.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Time (s)<math id="S4.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Speedup<math id="S4.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LPIPS<math id="S4.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SSIM<math id="S4.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">PSNR<math id="S4.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.8.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.8.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="6"><span id="S4.T2.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">SkyReels-V2</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.8.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.8.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.12,0.30)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.12</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.30</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.12,0.30)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S4.T2.8.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">353.11</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">4.11<math id="S4.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.1723</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.7581</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.8.4.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">23.17</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.8.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.8.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S4.T2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.15,0.36)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.15</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.36</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.15,0.36)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S4.T2.8.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">326.21</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">4.45<math id="S4.T2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.1798</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.7460</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">22.74</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.8.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.8.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S4.T2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.18,0.42)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.18</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.42</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.18,0.42)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S4.T2.8.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">307.34</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.8.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.8.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">4.73<math id="S4.T2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
